/*
	RMSTEST 1 — does avoid_forest_zone apply to a tight group's CENTRE or to
	each MEMBER?

	The guide contradicts itself. Under set_tight_grouping (guide:2122) it
	lists avoid_forest_zone among constraints that "apply only to the center
	of the group". Under avoid_forest_zone's own entry (guide:2569) it says
	"if the objects are grouped, distance will apply to the individual group
	members", unconditionally. docs/preview-design.md Sec.6.6 picks the
	per-attribute entry, so it predicts MEMBER.

	HOW IT DISCRIMINATES
	Each player gets a 15x15 grass clearing (base_size 7, growth target
	already met so it cannot expand) surrounded by forest. avoid_forest_zone 6
	is then geometrically impossible for a 5x5 tight group's outer members —
	they sit 2 tiles from centre, so they would need a clearing radius of 8 —
	but it is satisfiable for the group's CENTRE, which only needs radius 6.

	READ IT LIKE THIS
	  GOLD present (a 5x5 block of gold piles)  -> CENTRE. guide:2122 wins,
	                                               preview-design Sec.6.6 is
	                                               WRONG and needs reverting.
	  GOLD absent                               -> MEMBER. Sec.6.6 confirmed.

	The single STONE pile is a CONTROL with the same avoid_forest_zone 6 and
	no grouping. It must always appear. If stone is missing too, the map
	failed for an unrelated reason and this run tells us nothing.

	RUN ON: Tiny, 4 players. Four clearings = four samples.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
base_terrain WATER

create_player_lands
{
	terrain_type GRASS
	base_size 7
	number_of_tiles 1
	border_fuzziness 0
	circle_radius 33
}

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

/* THE TEST: 25 objects, tight, avoid_forest_zone 6 */
create_object GOLD
{
	number_of_objects 25
	set_tight_grouping
	set_gaia_object_only
	set_place_for_every_player
	avoid_forest_zone 6
}

/* THE CONTROL: same avoidance, ungrouped. Must always appear. */
create_object STONE
{
	number_of_objects 1
	set_gaia_object_only
	set_place_for_every_player
	avoid_forest_zone 6
}
